      "style": {
        "borderRadius": 28,
        "borderWidth": 4,
        "shadow": "xl",
        "glass": true,
        "gradient": true,
        "background": "linear-gradient(135deg,#8E24AA,#5E35B1)",
        "borderColor": "#CE93D8",
        "color": "#ffffff"
      },
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "markdown": "## 🔥 What Moves the Plates?\n\nHeat escaping from Earth’s interior drives slow motion within the mantle. Plate movement is also influenced by:\n\n- **Slab pull:** dense oceanic crust sinks and pulls a plate behind it.\n- **Ridge push:** elevated crust near ocean ridges slides outward under gravity.\n- **Mantle flow:** slowly moving rock transfers energy beneath the plates.\n\nMost plates move only a few centimeters per year, roughly the pace at which fingernails grow.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1784925556112,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
