      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "markdown": "## 💥 Convergent Boundary\n\nTwo plates move **toward each other**.\n\nAn oceanic plate may sink beneath another plate in a process called **subduction**, producing trenches and volcanic arcs. When two continental plates collide, neither sinks easily, so the crust crumples upward into mountains.\n\n**Common features**\n\n- Deep-ocean trenches\n- Volcanoes\n- Mountain ranges\n- Powerful earthquakes",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1784925556112,
