        "color": "#ffffff"
      },
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "markdown": "## 🌋 A Restless Planet\n\nPlate boundaries form a connected global system. Crust is created at divergent boundaries, transformed through collisions, and recycled into the mantle at subduction zones.\n\n### The grand cycle\n\n**Mantle heat → plate motion → boundary interactions → earthquakes, volcanoes, mountains, and changing oceans**\n\nThe continents beneath our feet are not fixed scenery. They are passengers on a planetary machine that has been remodeling Earth for billions of years.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1784925556112,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
